\section{Complexity}
Building the masks and adjacency sets costs $O(n^2)$ bit-set operations on
$L$-bit (respectively $n$-bit) words. Listing blocks needs $O(n^2)$ tests of
$\N(a)\cap\N(b)$. By Lemma~\ref{lem:few} there are $m\le 2n$ blocks, hence at most
$2n$ anchors. For one anchor, $Q$ and $T$ cost $O(n\log n)$ and the DP examines
all pairs of blocks, $O(m^2)=O(n^2)$. Total
\[
 \boxed{T(n)=O(n^3)\ \text{time},\qquad S(n)=O(n^2)\ \text{bits of space}}
\]
(plus $O(nL)$ bits for the minute masks, a constant for fixed $L=1440$).
Section~\ref{sec:live} gives an empirical check.

